{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.branching_dimension_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.branching_dimension_check","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L242-L245","doc":"Dimension cross-check: the two rank-one isotypic pieces exhaust\n`dim V_(2,1) = 2`, matching the `branchingH3H2 1 ·` row `(1, 1)` of the\nFrobenius lepton–meson bridge table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.res_sign_multiplicity_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.res_sign_multiplicity_one","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L204-L240","doc":"**⟨Res^{S₃}_{S₂} V_(2,1), V_(1,1)⟩ = 1** (sign counterpart).  Every\ns₁-anti-invariant vector automatically lies in the Specht module and is\na unique `R`-multiple of `w₋ = (1, −1, 0)`.  The no-2-torsion hypothesis\n`htf` is the weakest sufficient assumption (the statement fails in\ncharacteristic 2), carried explicitly per the\n`MilnorSignRepObstruction` convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.res_trivial_multiplicity_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.res_trivial_multiplicity_one","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L174-L202","doc":"**⟨Res^{S₃}_{S₂} V_(2,1), V_(2)⟩ = 1** (uniqueness half).  Every\ns₁-invariant vector of the Specht module is a UNIQUE `R`-multiple of\n`w₊ = (1, 1, −2)`: the trivial-isotypic component of the restriction is\nfree of rank one on `w₊`.  Combined with `wPlus_sumZero` +\n`wPlus_fixed` + `wPlus_ne_zero` (existence), this is the\nmultiplicity-one branching of the Frobenius lepton–meson bridge, proved\nrather than tabulated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L165-L170","doc":"`w₋ ≠ 0` whenever `R` is nontrivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L157-L163","doc":"`w₊ ≠ 0` whenever `R` is nontrivial — the invariant subspace is genuinely\nnonzero, so the multiplicity is exactly one, not at most one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_anti","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L143-L155","doc":"`w₋` is s₁-anti-invariant (existence half of the sign multiplicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L129-L141","doc":"`w₊` is s₁-invariant (existence half of multiplicity one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_sumZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_sumZero","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L123-L127","doc":"`w₋` lies in the Specht module: `1 + (−1) + 0 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_sumZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_sumZero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L117-L121","doc":"`w₊` lies in the Specht module: `1 + 1 + (−2) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_two","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L112-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_one","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L107-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L102-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_two","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L98-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L94-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L90-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wMinus","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L86-L88","doc":"The sign-isotypic (antisymmetric-channel) generator\n`w₋ = (1, −1, 0)` of the Specht module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.wPlus","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The trivial-isotypic (symmetric-channel) generator\n`w₊ = (1, 1, −2)` of the Specht module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.funext_fin3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.funext_fin3","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L71-L78","doc":"Function extensionality over `Fin 3`, stated at the three literals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.sumZero_permAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.sumZero_permAct","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L59-L69","doc":"The Specht module is an S₃-subrepresentation: the sum-zero condition is\npreserved by every relabeling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.permAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.permAct","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L55-L57","doc":"The S₃ relabeling action on the permutation module `Fin 3 → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.SumZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.SumZero","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtBranchingMultiplicityOne.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Membership in the concrete Specht module `V_(2,1)`: the sum-zero\nsubspace of the permutation module `Fin 3 → R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}